{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe agentic plan-review engine (ADR 0123) signs a PASS for a run that read no code. `plan_review/agentic_verdict.py::adapt_findings` sets `coverage.llm_ran = True` and builds the verdict from the findings list alone. Nothing in `agentic.py`, `agentic_verdict.py` or the `agentic_review` step of `llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml` checks how many tool calls the agent made. So an agent that answers `{\"findings\": []}` at once, with 0 `read_file`/`list_directory`/`search_files` calls, gets a non-blocking PASS and a certified plan-review attestation that the claim gate accepts.\n\nThe pipeline engine has no equivalent hole: every routed criterion chunk must return, and missing coverage resolves INDETERMINATE.\n\nThis is a silent-approval path in a gate.\n\n## Plan\nHow the count is available: a production agent call records its run shape on `result[\"_usage\"]` (`runner_support._merge_success_run_shape` merges `usage_log.shape_only(run_shape(...))`). The shape includes `tool_calls` (every tool call) and `distinct_fetches`, which `usage_log.fetch_target` fills only for `read_file`, `search_files` and `list_directory` calls, the code-reading tools. The workflow recorder keeps each succeeded step's outputs, so the `agentic_review` step's `outputs._usage` carries both (`gate_dispatch._consumed_diagnostic` already reads `_usage` the same way).\n\nThe rule counts **code reads** (`distinct_fetches`), not all tool calls, so a run that only calls `show_ticket` or `resolve_symbol` still counts as having read no code.\n\n1. **RED first.** In `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`, with a fake runner whose agentic answer carries `_usage`:\n   - `_usage = {\"requests\": 1, \"tool_calls\": 0, \"distinct_fetches\": []}`, zero findings: INDETERMINATE, `signature.signed` False, `plan_review_status` `unsigned` before and after (no attestation written), `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`, `coverage.resolution_class == \"FIX_AGENT_DESIGN\"`, `coverage.diagnostic` carries `tool_calls` 0 and a `message` naming the 3 code-reading tools.\n   - `_usage = {\"requests\": 2, \"tool_calls\": 1, \"distinct_fetches\": []}` (a `show_ticket`-only run): INDETERMINATE and unsigned.\n   - `_usage = {\"requests\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 10}` with no shape keys (the shape reducer failed): INDETERMINATE and unsigned (fail closed); the diagnostic omits `tool_calls`.\n   - `_usage` with 1 `distinct_fetches` entry and zero findings: PASS and signed, as today.\n   - `_usage` absent or `{}` (the offline fake runners, including `FakeRunner`'s structured `{}`): unchanged, so existing tests keep passing.\n   Also in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py`, drive the real `PydanticAIRunner` with a pydantic-ai `FunctionModel` in structured mode: a run that answers without a tool call yields `_usage[\"distinct_fetches\"] == []`, and one that calls `read_file` first yields 1 entry, proving the production producer fills the field the check reads.\n   Confirm the first 3 fail before the fix.\n2. **Fix.** In `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`: add `STEP_AGENTIC_REVIEW = \"agentic_review\"` to the central step-id vocabulary and to `_PLAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED_STEP_IDS`, so a rename in `plan-review.yaml` fails loudly at dispatch instead of silently disabling the check. Add `agentic_unread_error(rec) -> BaseException | None`: it finds the succeeded `STEP_AGENTIC_REVIEW` record; when its `outputs._usage` is a non-empty dict whose `distinct_fetches` is missing or empty, it returns an `LLMRunnerError` carrying `LLMOutcome(FIX_AGENT_DESIGN, sanitize_diagnostic({requests, tool_calls, message, exception_type}), retryable=False)`; otherwise `None`.\n3. In `gate_dispatch`'s plan-review success branch, before returning the terminal verdict: when `engine == \"agentic\"` and `agentic_unread_error(rec)` returns an error, return `_degraded_plan_review_verdict(...)` with it. That is the path every failed agentic run already takes (budget and tool-loop exhaustion are FIX_AGENT_DESIGN there too), so the verdict is an unsigned INDETERMINATE with `resolution_class`, `retryable` and the diagnostic on coverage. Like those failures, it carries `llm_unavailable: True`, the flag `degrade_cause_flags` sets for any non-input-rejection error. A floor-blocked or not-claimable review never runs `agentic_review`, so it is unaffected.\n4. ADR 0123 §3: add that an agentic run with no code read resolves INDETERMINATE (FIX_AGENT_DESIGN) and is never signed.\n\nBehavior is unconditional: no config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] An agentic run that read no code (no `read_file`/`search_files`/`list_directory` call), or whose reported `_usage` lacks the run shape, resolves INDETERMINATE through the existing degraded-verdict path with `resolution_class` FIX_AGENT_DESIGN, and writes no attestation, pinned by tests.\n- [ ] An agentic run with at least 1 code read still PASSes and signs, and offline runners that report no usage are unchanged, pinned by tests.\n- [ ] A real-runner test shows `_usage.distinct_fetches` is empty without a code read and has 1 entry after a `read_file` call.\n- [ ] `agentic_review` is in `_PLAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED_STEP_IDS`.\n- [ ] ADR 0123 §3 states the no-code-read rule.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794565729023104001,"uuid":"ff25b072-a852-4ee5-8768-a9fdc9b98860"}